{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Accidental Humanitarians"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Helping Out"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "  Describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ethical dilemma"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a situation in which a difficult choice has to be made about what is right and what is wrong"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I guess I'm just having a bit of an ethical dilemma."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about social issues and moral dilemmas. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "care package"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a package containing goods such as food and clothing for the needy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So long as we keep sending care packages, we won't see any lasting progress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lasting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describing something that exists for a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So long as we keep sending care packages, we won't see any lasting progress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "governance"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way that countries are run"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The effects of colonization, years of poor governance, and civil war have taken their toll."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take a toll "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cause damage or suffering"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The effects of colonization, years of poor governance, and civil war have taken their toll."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "disaster relief "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "money or goods given to people after they have been affected by a natural disaster"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I guess I'm just focused on this news report I heard about disaster relief."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "corruption"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "dishonest or illegal behavior"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a lot of corruption within the government."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "misappropriation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "inappropriate or illegal management money or goods"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It showed so much corruption and misappropriation of funds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le07ob05aud08"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le07ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Will/Won't in the If-Clause"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use the first conditional to talk about possibilities in the present or future - things which might happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A first conditional sentence consists of two clauses, an \"if\" clause and a main clause:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">If you study hard, you will pass the test.</span><br/>= It's possible that you will pass the test on the condition that you study hard."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You sometimes use will and won't in the if-clause with the meanings of refusal (won't), polite request (will), or strong disapproval at someone's insistence on doing something (will): "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Refusal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">won't </span>go, there is nothing you can do about it.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Request\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If <span class=\\\"strong\\\">you'll hold </span>this end, I'll take the other one. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Insistence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If <span class=\\\"strong\\\">you will drive </span>so fast, you must expect to have accidents.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you'll just take a seat right there, I'll be right with you."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you'll just hold on a second, I'll dig up the numbers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If they won't change, then there's really nothing we can do about it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If he won't do it, I will. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adverb Clauses of Condition"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Adverb clauses can put a condition on an action. You use the conjunctions <span class=\"italic\">if</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> whether</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> provided that </span>and <span class=\"italic\">unless </span>to introduce the condition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">If I like it</span>, I will get it.<br/><span class=\"strong\">If you heat ice</span>, it turns to water.<br/><span class=\"strong\">If it rains</span>, we will stay at home.<br/>You can come, <span class=\"strong\">if you want to</span>. <br/>You won't succeed <span class=\"strong\">unless you work hard</span>. <br/>You will miss the bus <span class=\"strong\">unless you leave now</span>. <br/>There will be no problem <span class=\"strong\">provided that you stay quiet</span> <br/>You will have to take the medicine <span class=\"strong\">whether you like it or not</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes you can omit the conjunction <span class=\"italic\">if</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Were the child mine</span>, I would have taken it to a doctor. (= If the child were mine, I would have taken it to a doctor.)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Should you meet my brother</span>, tell him that I have gone to the railway station. (= If you meet my brother, tell him that I have gone to the railway station.)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Unless we help the local people through education, we won't see any real change."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we don't help, they'll just suffer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Provided that we focus on education, I am sure we will continue to see incremental improvements."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write the following statement on a piece of paper: Sending aid to foreign countries does not help development."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner or group, write down a list of pros (supporting the statement) and cons (opposed to the statement)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find at least three facts to support your views."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Split up and debate the statement."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I discuss an ethical dilemma."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a list of pros and cons."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I research facts to support my point of view."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I debate an ethical dilemma."}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le07ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le07ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le07ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: Hi, Amy. If you'll just take a seat right there, I'll be right with you ... now, what's on your mind?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I've been thinking. I know that in the short term we're helping out, but are we really providing a long-term solution for these people?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: Of course we are ...\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I guess I'm just having a bit of an ethical dilemma. I mean, so long as we keep sending care packages, we won't see any lasting progress.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le07ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: That's exactly why we don't send care packages. We realized a long time ago that unless we help the local people through education, we won't see any real change.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: Isn't it a bit arrogant to think that they even need our help? I mean, if we don't help, they'll just suffer. Is that the idea?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: Not at all. The effects of colonization, years of poor governance, and civil war have taken their toll. It's our responsibility to help undo some of the mistakes of the past.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: But how do we know that it's working?", "id": 2, "time": "27000", "image": "engenn10le07ob05re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: If you'll just hold on a second, I'll dig up the numbers ... here they are. You see? In our community, employment is up and the infection rate is down. Provided that we focus on education, I am sure we will continue to see incremental improvements.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I guess I'm just focused on this news report I heard about disaster relief. It showed so much corruption and misappropriation of funds.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: Those NGOs are outdated. If they won't change, then there's really nothing we can do about it. We've got to focus on ourselves.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Amy</span>: I agree. In the interest of transparency, why don't convince the director to post all of our cash flow online.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Candice</span>: What a great idea! If he won't do it, I will.", "id": 3, "time": "59300", "image": "engenn10le07ob05re2img05.jpg"}]}}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about social issues and moral dilemmas."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "  I can make polite requests or express disapproval or refusal using if. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about under what conditions something is done. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Does sending aid to developing countries help long-term development? Why? Why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How can we combat corruption in relief efforts?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Let's have an ethical debate!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nAmy <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">raises</span> a few interesting points.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}]}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"type": "text", "tip_id": 0, "content": " To <span class=\"italic\">\"raise a point\"</span> means to put it forth as a topic of discussion."}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.\n"}]}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": 